=== T3.6: the LK gradient covariance -- fused against composed ===
target: not aarch64 -- INDICATIVE ONLY. Every variant here is popcount-bound,
        and the x86 popcount lowering (X-7: a libgcc CALL per word on the
        shipped baseline) can change the ranking outright.
640x480, 200 keypoints, one window each -- the LK access pattern of
ARCHITECTURE 7.5. The rule this is measured against is in this file's
header, written before measuring.

"composed/fused" > 1.00x means the FUSED entry point T3.6 ships is faster,
confirming D-15 axis 2 at this level. "plane/4arg" > 1.00x means the
precomputed selector plane is faster than the four-argument form -- which it
is expected to be, and is the speed T3.6 spends to save the plane.

